      "id": "6jrd73e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Radius and General Facts about the Earth"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth's structure is broadly divided into three main concentric layers: Crust, Mantle, and Core.",
        "Information regarding the Earth's interior is derived from direct sources (volcanic materials, deep drilling) and indirect sources (seismic waves, density variations).",
        "The Crust consists of two distinct types: Continental Crust (composed mainly of SIAL - Silica & Aluminium) and Oceanic Crust (composed of SIMA - Silica & Magnesium).",
        "The Mantle contains critical functional regions, including the semi-molten Asthenosphere which enables tectonic movement.",
        "Transitions between internal layers are defined by key boundary zones known as seismic discontinuities."
      ],
      "id": "zbm9agv"
    },
